.he "mwformat (1)                 9/28/26                 mwformat (1)"
.fo "                               -#-"
.in 5
.rm 65
.bd
NAME
.in +5
.br
.bd
mwformat
- format a Morrow HD-DMA hard disk
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SYNTAX
.in +5
.br
.bd
mwformat device [ track ]
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
Mwformat runs the controller's format-track command across a drive, one
track per ioctl, printing a line as each track is done.  The device node
names the drive and the model, by the type bits of its minor number, and
the model's geometry is how many tracks are walked.  A format blanks the
disk, headers and data, so the label and any filesystem go with it and
mkfs follows.
.sp
With a track argument, only that one track is formatted.
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
EXAMPLE
.in +5
.br
.bd
mwformat /dev/m16a
.sp 2
.in -5
.bd
SEE ALSO
.in +5
.br
mkfs (1)
